        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>How much does a LifeSpan treadmill cost?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              On LifeSpan’s US store on 26 November 2026, its under-desk treadmills cost $1,199 (TR1200Pro Glow-Up), $1,399 (TX6-GlowUp) and $1,699 (TR5000B Pro+ GlowUp), and its treadmill desk sets $2,048 to $2,748. Its folding treadmills, last listed at $1,199 to $4,999, were all sold out.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is the LifeSpan TX6 treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              $1,399 on LifeSpan and on Amazon on 26 November 2026, against a $1,499 compare-at price. We recorded $1,499 at LifeSpan on 14 October, and an independent tracker recorded $1,299 at LifeSpan and Amazon in February 2026.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>How much is a LifeSpan TR1200 treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              The current TR1200Pro Glow-Up under-desk treadmill was $1,199 on LifeSpan on 26 November 2026, against $1,299 compare-at, and on pre-order. The TR1200PRO Omni desk set was $2,048. The older TR1200i folding treadmill was last listed at $1,199 but sold out.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does LifeSpan still sell folding treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Not in November 2026. The TR1200i, TR2000i, TR3000i, TR4000i and TR5500iM folding treadmills and the TR6000i and TR7000iM commercial treadmills were all marked sold out on LifeSpan’s US store on 26 November, and its Fitness menu no longer listed treadmills.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does LifeSpan charge for shipping?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Shipping was free on US orders over $1,300 on 26 November 2026, which covers every LifeSpan treadmill and desk set except the $1,199 TR1200Pro on its own. Free shipping excludes Alaska, Hawaii, Puerto Rico and Canada, and LifeSpan lists a $149 Standard Delivery upgrade.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you return a LifeSpan treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Only on LifeSpan’s terms. Its policy says it ended 30-day returns in February 2025; once an order ships, a US return costs a 20% restocking fee plus $350 shipping. Orders from 25 November to 15 December are exchange or store credit only, until 15 January.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a LifeSpan treadmill worth the money?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              For long daily walking at a desk, often yes: 20-inch belts, 6 to 9-hour daily ratings and a 10-year frame warranty are rare among walking pads. For running, no; Horizon and Sole sell full folding running treadmills for about $1,100.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
